# File contexts for the qdistro session manager.
#
# Phase 1 (0.1.0): labels the daemon .py so systemd's exec triggers the
# init_daemon_domain transition into qdistro_sessmgr_t. The .py is
# installed mode 0755 with a `#!/usr/bin/env python3` shebang and the
# unit's ExecStart points at the script directly (not /usr/bin/python3 +
# arg). The kernel takes the transition decision on the FIRST execve
# target — the labelled .py — so the daemon lands in qdistro_sessmgr_t
# regardless of the interpreter's own label (same reasoning as the
# broker/pwd .fc files).
#
# Only the exec is labelled in Phase 1. The session manager's persistent
# state (silos.yaml, session_audit.sqlite, the export-back lineage store
# under /var/lib/qdistro/lineage/) and runtime dirs stay under their
# existing types until the Phase-2 audit2allow harvest decides which need
# dedicated types — keeping the permissive-rollout surface minimal and the
# relabel list short. (The lineage store joins this deferred list: the
# enforcing-mode allow rules for qdistro_sessmgr_t writing the sqlite +
# WAL/SHM there come from that harvest, which needs a console-driven
# enforcing VM — the headless lane runs permissive.)

/usr/libexec/qdistro/qdistro_session_manager\.py    --  gen_context(system_u:object_r:qdistro_sessmgr_exec_t,s0)
